WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.240
Here's how to put a second layout on one controller with a shift layer,

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.670
and a ring of commands on a stick with a radial menu.

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.070
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.650
On the controller's Mappings tab, click Shift Layer.

5
00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:18.951
Name the layer, then pick what turns it on.

6
00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:20.631
Here, it's the left shoulder.

7
00:00:22.472 --> 00:00:25.072
Hold keeps the layer on while you hold the button.

8
00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:30.212
Tick Inherit Unmapped Targets, so every button you leave alone keeps its usual job.

9
00:00:30.252 --> 00:00:31.702
Then save.

10
00:00:32.947 --> 00:00:35.597
The layer gets its own tab above the grid.

11
00:00:36.047 --> 00:00:38.917
A row you bind on it works only while the layer is on.

12
00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.620
Now the Menus tab.

13
00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:42.400
Click Add.

14
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.570
The new menu is a radial ring on the right stick, with four cells.

15
00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:51.342
Give each cell a label and a binding.

16
00:00:51.772 --> 00:00:52.742
This one says Map.

17
00:00:54.477 --> 00:00:57.387
Open its binding list, and choose Controller Button.

18
00:00:57.737 --> 00:00:59.867
Then pick the button it presses: Back.

19
00:01:01.152 --> 00:01:04.372
With the pad in hand, hold the left shoulder for the layer,

20
00:01:04.412 --> 00:01:06.842
and push the right stick to open the menu.

21
00:01:07.412 --> 00:01:09.922
Point at a cell, and click the stick to fire it.

22
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:14.727
Find more guides at padforge.org.
